by nicolas-grekas at 2026-08-15T11:54:52Z

I pushed a rework to make this merge-ready. @Jean85 please review what I changed, since the branch now differs quite a bit from your last push:

- rebased on 8.2, squashed into a single commit under your authorship;
- renamed the directory to `Bridge/MongoDb` and aligned class names with the sibling bridges: `MongoDbTransportFactory`, `MongoDbReceiver`, `MongoDbSender`, `MongoDbReceivedStamp`, `MongoDbSessionStamp`;
- replaced the container-based factory with a plain-DSN one: `Connection::fromDsn()` creates the `MongoDB\Client` itself, and an already-built `Client` can be passed as argument. The `mongodb://` and `mongodb+srv://` schemes are handled, transport settings are skimmed from the query string and everything else is passed through to the driver, following the `MongoDbStore` precedent in the Lock component;
- removed the DocumentEnhancer feature, as suggested by @GromNaN; it can come back in a dedicated PR;
- implemented the `$fetchSize` hidden argument of `ReceiverInterface::get()`, which 8.2 deprecates not defining. Messages are still claimed one by one since each claim is an atomic `findOneAndUpdate`;
- moved the session-stamp lookup into the sender, so `Connection::send()` takes data instead of the envelope;
- made the clock a nullable PSR-20 `ClockInterface` and used it consistently: `send()` previously created `new \DateTime()` and ignored the injected clock;
- switched to the Messenger exceptions, stopped emitting `'session' => null` in write options, and dropped the `facile-it_messenger_index` index name;
- fixed the unit tests (they passed the clock where the enhancer array was expected, so the suite was red) and kept the stubs file: the tests mock the real library classes when they are installed and fall back to the stubs otherwise, like the Lock component does;
- added `MongoDbTransportIntegrationTest` covering send/get/ack, reject, delay, redelivery, all/find, session and setup; it runs against the `mongodb` service in the integration workflow;
- wired the monorepo and the framework: `splitsh.json`, factory registration in FrameworkBundle, the "composer require symfony/mongodb-messenger" hint in Messenger's `TransportFactory`, `mongodb` in the unit-test workflow extensions, and the integration workflow now installs `mongodb/mongodb` (the pinned ext-mongodb 1.12.0 could not install the library, so the pin is gone);
- composer requirements per the review: `ext-mongodb: ^1.21|^2.0` and `mongodb/mongodb: ^1.21|^2.0`, which is what `getCollection()` needs; also LICENSE year, changelog and README.

Left out on purpose: resolving a pre-built `Client` from the container by service id. No other bridge has DI plumbing like that, programmatic reuse is covered by the `$client` argument of `fromDsn()`, and bundle integrations can build on it.

Thanks for offering the package to core, and for your patience.

